 	 * timer interrupt yet, so a pass that blocks on a cross-thread wait can
 	 * never be observed or woken. Run the pass inline on the boot thread where
 	 * the boot-progress marks name the exact step it stops on.
+	 *
+	 * 2026-11-03: the deferred pass was still reachable through a cooperative
+	 * thread switch, and switching to the inline one is the only change that
+	 * demonstrably moved ArmDTPlatform::configure from "finished" to "never
+	 * entered" (iPadOS line: cfg=1 asynchronously, cfg=48 right after the
+	 * switch, and the whole iOS 16.5 line has read cfg=0). So the choice is a
+	 * boot argument now instead of a rebuild: r11-root-async=1 runs the stock
+	 * deferred pass, 0 (default) keeps the inline one. Both paths paint the
+	 * same ROOT counters in IOService.cpp, so either way one boot still says
+	 * whether the root pass ran and what findDrivers() returned for it.
